[{"id":2560409037,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6YnL3N","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The change here is definitely more accurate than what's there currently, especially considering that this is already being called a collision normal in `ShapeCast3D.get_collision_normal`, which returns this exact normal.\r\n\r\nThe documentation for these result fields seems to be a bit ambiguous though, with it referring to the hit object as \"the colliding object\", \"the intersecting object\" and \"the object\" all at once.\r\n\r\nI would probably rephrase the documentation for the normal to say that it's the collision normal of the query shape, since it describes the direction in which to move the query shape away from the collision and not the hit object. I would probably also specify which direction it's pointing in, for those who might not be familiar with this kind of physics speak.\r\n\r\nLastly, we might as well normalize \"the colliding object\", \"the intersecting object\" and \"the object\" as just \"the intersecting object\", since that might be a little bit less ambiguous, but would also line up better with most of the 